[470.63, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 3 report: Depth**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rebuilt the loop as a designed edit**:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Anticipation: the inward spiral accelerates and the camera pulls in.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Impact: a detonation at 8.4s with a flash, camera kick and slight chromatic aberration.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Follow-through: a rainbow shockwave shell and ring. Each particle is released as the front reaches it,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with a small overshoot.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Pointer**:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Gravity well that swirls orbits around the pointer and pulls them toward it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Glowing trail that fades from gold to pink.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Click shockwave.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A ghost pointer that moves by itself until you move yours.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Page opens on the detonation** (loop time 8.5s) and then plays through the shockwave.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Colour grading and quality**:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - ACES tone mapping and a vignette.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Particle count scaled by device, plus an adaptive step-down if frames run slow.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Test tools** are in `.ambition/tools/`: Playwright capture with a controllable clock, a contact sheet\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  builder, a seam diff and a pointer path script.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **The first version's implosion was a full-screen white blob from about 6.5s to 9.0s.** About 90,000\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  additive particles piled onto one spot. I had said earlier it was about 60,000 particles. The real count is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  about 90,000.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - My first rebuild had the same problem. It took three render-and-look rounds to fix: collapsed particles\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  now dim sharply, a controlled core sprite carries the white-hot point, bloom is lower and the flash decays\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  quickly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Seam check:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The 9.9833s to 0.0s step differs by 4.09, against a noise floor of about 3.0.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - That floor is the difference between two frames 0.2ms apart.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Ordinary one-frame steps elsewhere range from 1.0 to 7.7.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - So the seam is indistinguishable from noise. It is not bit-identical.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Pointer path:** the trail and the orbit bending show up in the scripted run. How the pointer feels is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  yours to judge.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - There were no console errors in any run.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I didn't compare numerically against the first version's collapse, because its whiteout makes that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  comparison meaningless. The contact sheets show the difference.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Frame-time check: I haven't run it. Software rendering gives only a rough number, so your browser's frame\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rate is the better test.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The contact sheet of the final 5 to 10s window is `.ambition/shots/sheet3.png`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Snapshots are in `.ambition/first/` (the original) and `.ambition/steps/3/` (this version).\u001b[0m\r\n"]
