[492.097, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 4/8 · Challenge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions I'm making, riskiest first**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | # | Assumption | Set by | Depends on |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 1 | The core flash looks the same at every screen size. | Me: sizes in raw pixels, up to 800. | GPU point-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  size limits, DPR |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 2 | The scene frames well on any screen shape. | Me: camera distance fixed at 48. | Aspect ratio |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 3 | Real time wraps at 10s, with the page opening at 85% of the loop. | Me and you | Real clock, not my\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  test clock |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 4 | The click shockwave works. | Me | I never tested it |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 5 | The 3.0 \"noise floor\" is harmless. | Me, assumed | Unknown source |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'm testing these against the real page now, starting with 1 and 3.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
