[788.106, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 5 report: Range**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did.** I borrowed one concrete method from each field and applied it to `solar-implosion.html`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Colourist:** the singularity is now white-hot with a violet halo. It was beige before, which doesn't\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  read as neon.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Game-feel designer:** clicks send a ripple out from the cursor ring, and touch devices get touch wording\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  in the hint.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Motion and demoscene artist, with a sound-design idea:** a short pre-impact dip. It turned out to add\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  little (see below).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Red team:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Support for `prefers-reduced-motion`: the flash is about 30% as strong, with no camera shake or zoom\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  punch.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - If three.js or WebGL fails to load, the page now shows a clear message and keeps your normal cursor.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Before, you got a black page and no cursor. I tested both cases.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The flash is softer for everyone.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The flash was a full-screen near-white strobe: mean luminance jumped from 5% to 98% in about two frames.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  It happens once per loop, so it was under the three-per-second rule, but it was harsh.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - After the change, normal mode peaks at 84% and rises over about four frames. The biggest one-frame step is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  36%, down from 75%. In reduced-motion mode the peak is 23%.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The flash is still bright. It's the loop's climax, and cutting it further would weaken the impact. If\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  you'd rather have it gentler, say so and I'll lower the peak.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The pre-impact dip is mostly redundant. By then the collapsed particles are already near-black (frame\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  luminance 4% to 6%), so the dark moment before the hit exists without it. It's harmless, so I left it in.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I didn't build sound. A sound designer would add the biggest impact, but I can't judge audio by ear, and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  page that autoplays sound is a harm of its own.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course.** I took the flash softening as the \"edge\" because it affects both shareability and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  safety. I didn't touch pointer feel or the frame rate; you judge those. The latest contact sheet is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `.ambition/shots/sheet6.png`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Snapshots are in `.ambition/first/` (the original) and `steps/3/`, `4/` and `5/` (this version).\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[788.215, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 6 of pushing the work further: Judge. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 6/8 · Judge`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +17 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[826.745, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 6/8 · Judge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The check I'm holding it to is a script, not my opinion: `.ambition/tools/judge.mjs`. It renders the real\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  page in Chrome with a controllable clock and scores every promise in the restatement. Each check gives a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  pass or fail, and where a number exists the first version is measured the same way. Before writing it, I did\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a cold read of the page's only copy, the hint line, and found a problem. The hint is `#9af` at 60% opacity\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  on near-black. That works out to about 3.8:1 contrast, below the 4.5:1 AA threshold for small text. I'm\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fixing that, and exposing particle count so the device-scaling check can read it.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
