[2060.223, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 7 report: Stretch**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The stretch target missed, and I restored the version from before the attempt. `solar-implosion.html` is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  identical to the pre-step version, with 18 of 18 checks passing. A snapshot is in `.ambition/steps/7/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did.** The target was 3× the particles (about 275,000) at no more frame cost than the current ~92,000. I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  measured where the time goes, then tried culling, a quarter-resolution bloom and a 1.5× default.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Where the time goes:** the shader math is cheap. The cost is per point rasterised, at about 0.065ms per\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  thousand points. Bloom adds a fixed 5 to 8ms. This is software rendering, so a real GPU will behave very\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  differently.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **The target breaks at 3×.** Mean cost across the loop is 22.4ms at 1× and 37.5ms at 3×. The best I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  reached was about 32ms at 3×.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Two partial wins, neither kept:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Dropping most of the particles stacked in the singularity (keeping a quarter at four times the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  brightness) saves only about 4%, and hue was unchanged.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Quarter-resolution bloom saves about 20%, but it leaves blocky, square-edged halos and blotches that my\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  metrics didn't catch. Only looking at the frames showed them. This is why I reverted.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Density costs colour.** At 1.5× particles the mean saturation and hue variety dropped, because more\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  overlapping additive light goes white. I could win the saturation back by pushing the grade harder, but that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  would trade the neon look for a number.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Where the fallback stands.** Your fallback is intact: 60fps-class smoothness through the existing\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  adaptive step-down, with particle count scaled to the device (about 92,000 on desktop, about 46,000 on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  mobile).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course.** I kept the `?q=` URL override, which lets you set a particle multiplier for experiments,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  for example `?q=1.5`. It has no effect on a normal visit.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The measurement tools (`loopcost.mjs`, `fps.mjs`, `hues.mjs`) and the spike variants stay under\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `.ambition/`. The check misses blockiness, so I'd want a guard for it in the final step.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
