[2175.89, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ## Plan and report\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Plan (as delivered).** The ask is a single-page three.js piece: a vivid, neon, interactive solar-system\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  particle implosion that loops seamlessly every 10 seconds. The goal beyond it is a showcase page that wows\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  on opening, with the implosion as the moment people replay and the pointer as the hook. The target is a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  collapse and rebirth that builds, hits a white-hot singularity and releases a colourful shockwave, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  physical gravity-well pointer with a fading trail, a striking opening and smooth frame rates. The approach\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  was a designed edit (anticipation, impact, follow-through) driven by one function of loop time, rendered in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  real Chrome and scored by `check/judge.mjs`. The stretch target was 3× the particles at the same cost, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  your 60fps-style smoothness is the fallback.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | You asked for | It became |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Vivid, neon, abstract | Saturated particles, bloom, a saturation boost in the grade pass, and a violet-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  white singularity. Measured saturation is 0.28, against 0.16 in the first version. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Solar system, particle implosion | Sun, eight planets, belt and dust, about 92,000 particles. Anticipation\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  spiral, singularity, then a rainbow shockwave that releases particles on arrival, with a bounce. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Pointer interactive | Gravity well that bends orbits, a glowing trail that fades, a click shockwave, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  cursor ripple and a self-playing ghost pointer until you move yours. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 10-second seamless loop | Exact period. The seam step is 6.5 against an ordinary median of 5.9. The page\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  opens just after the detonation. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | three.js, single page | One HTML file, with three.js loaded from unpkg. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version.** The final is better on every measure and worse on nothing I measured.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Measure | First version | Final |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Whiteout (frames over 70% luminance, of 100) | 31 to 32 | 1 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Mean saturation | 0.16 | 0.28 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Shockwave hue bins at 9s | 0 | 5 or 6 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Opening frame hue bins | 2 | 4 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Pointer trail, light added | +3.5 | +12.0 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The one raw number that is lower is the software-rendered frame rate, 46 fps against 53 fps. It is not a GPU\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  number.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check.** `npm run check` renders the real page in Chrome and returns 18 of 18 passing. It covers\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  single page, whiteout, black frames, saturation, shockwave colour, singularity, opening frame, exact period,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  seam, pointer trail, trail fade, orbit reaction, reduced-motion flash, climax size at three screen sizes,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  device scaling, CDN failure, hint contrast and console errors. I also looked at contact sheets at each\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  stage. The check cannot see blocky bloom or garish colour, which is why the sheet step stays.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch.** The target was 3× the particles at the same cost. It missed: about 32ms per frame at 3× against\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  22ms. The cost is per point rasterised, and it can't be removed without removing points. The two partial\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  wins did not hold up:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Quarter-resolution bloom caused blocky halos that only a visual check caught.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - 1.5× density washed the colour out.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I restored the pre-attempt version, so the final is unchanged by the stretch. The fallback stands.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in** (the check cannot see how the pointer feels, or the real GPU frame rate):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `check/judge.mjs`, `check/capture.mjs`, `check/sheet.mjs` and `check/package.json`: run `cd check && npm\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  install && npm run check` (about 75 seconds), then `npm run frames` and look at `.ambition/shots/now.png`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `CLAUDE.md`: how to run it, the evidence so far, and what not to retry.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `.claude/commands/neon-check.md`: the `/neon-check` project command.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions made.** None. You answered every question, and I didn't use my own judgement in place of an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  answer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Decisions left**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | # | Decision | Options | For / against | My pick | Owner, date |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 1 | Flash intensity | Keep (peak 83% luminance) · gentler (about 60%) | Keep: strongest impact. Gentler:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  safer for more viewers, less punch. | Keep, with reduced-motion support already on | You, by 2026-11-20 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 2 | Pointer feel | Keep the camera parallax · remove it | Keep: depth. Remove: the trail no longer drifts\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  on screen as the camera moves. | Keep until you've tried it | You, after trying it, by 2026-11-20 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 3 | Sound | Skip · opt-in toggle | Skip: nothing I can't verify. Toggle: adds weight to the impact, but\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  needs hearing it. | Skip | You, 2026-11-27 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 4 | Hosting | Keep the unpkg CDN · inline three.js | CDN: tiny file. Inline: works offline and removes a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  failure point, at about 700KB. | Inline before you publish it | You, before publishing |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 5 | Real GPU frame rate | Measure on your hardware | Software rendering can't tell me. Open the page and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  check the frame rate. | Do this first | You, by 2026-11-16 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The next check is `/neon-check` after any edit, run by whoever edits (you or me on request).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Metrics**\u001b[0m\r\n"]
